{"id":"mahabharata-3-146","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":146,"title":"षट्चत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 146 · Bhima goes for the saugandhika flower","summary":{"en":"The wind brings a thousand-petalled saugandhika lotus to Draupadi, and she asks Bhima to fetch more. Bhima storms up the mountain, scattering beasts and breaking trees, until his way is blocked by a great old monkey lying across the path, who tells him to eat fruit and turn back.","kn":"ಗಾಳಿ ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯ ಬಳಿಗೆ ಸಾವಿರ ದಳದ ಸೌಗಂಧಿಕ ಕಮಲವನ್ನು ತರುತ್ತದೆ, ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ತಾರೆಂದು ಅವಳು ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಭೀಮನು ಮೃಗಗಳನ್ನು ಚದುರಿಸಿ ಮರಗಳನ್ನು ಮುರಿಯುತ್ತಾ ಪರ್ವತವೇರುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದಾರಿಗಡ್ಡವಾಗಿ ಮಲಗಿದ ದೊಡ್ಡ ಮುದಿ ಕಪಿಯೊಂದು ಹಣ್ಣು ತಿಂದು ಹಿಂದಿರುಗೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"वायु द्रौपदी के पास सहस्रदल सौगन्धिक कमल लाती है, और वे भीम से और लाने को कहती हैं। भीम पशुओं को भगाते और वृक्ष तोड़ते हुए पर्वत पर चढ़ते हैं, जब तक मार्ग पर लेटा एक विशाल वृद्ध वानर उनका रास्ता नहीं रोक लेता और उन्हें फल खाकर लौट जाने को कहता है।","te":"గాలి ద్రౌపది వద్దకు వేయిరేకుల సౌగంధిక పద్మాన్ని తెస్తుంది, మరిన్ని తెమ్మని ఆమె భీముని అడుగుతుంది. భీముడు మృగాలను చెదరగొడుతూ చెట్లను విరుస్తూ పర్వతం ఎక్కుతాడు; దారికి అడ్డంగా పడుకున్న ఒక పెద్ద ముసలి వానరం పండ్లు తిని వెనక్కి వెళ్లమంటుంది.","ta":"காற்று திரௌபதியிடம் ஆயிரம் இதழ் ஸௌகந்திகத் தாமரையைக் கொண்டு வர, மேலும் கொண்டு வருமாறு அவள் பீமனைக் கேட்கிறாள். பீமன் விலங்குகளை விரட்டி மரங்களை முறித்தபடி மலையேற, வழியின் குறுக்கே படுத்திருந்த ஒரு பெரிய முதிய குரங்கு அவனைத் தடுத்துப் பழம் உண்டு திரும்பிச் செல்லுமாறு சொல்கிறது.","ml":"കാറ്റ് ആയിരം ഇതളുള്ള സൗഗന്ധിക താമര ദ്രൗപദിക്ക് കൊണ്ടുവരുന്നു; കൂടുതൽ കൊണ്ടുവരാൻ അവൾ ഭീമനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. ഭീമൻ മൃഗങ്ങളെ ചിതറിച്ചും മരങ്ങൾ ഒടിച്ചും പർവതം കയറുന്നു; വഴിയിൽ കുറുകെ കിടക്കുന്ന ഒരു വലിയ വൃദ്ധക്കുരങ്ങൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തടയുന്നു; പഴം കഴിച്ച് തിരിച്ചുപോകാൻ അത് ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.146; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तत्र ते पुरुषव्याघ्राः परमं शौचमास्थिताः ।\nषड्रात्रमवसन्वीरा धनंजयदिदृक्षया ।\nतस्मिन्विहरमाणाश्च रममाणाश्च पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tiger-like Pandavas stayed there six nights in strict purity, longing to see Arjuna, and they roamed and played in that lovely forest."}},{"n":2,"text":"मनोज्ञे काननवरे सर्वभूतमनोरमे ।\nपादपैः पुष्पविकचैः फलभारावनामितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was a charming, excellent wood that delighted every creature, its trees bright with blossoms and bent low under their fruit."}},{"n":3,"text":"शोभितं सर्वतोरम्यैः पुंस्कोकिलकुलाकुलैः ।\nस्निग्धपत्रैरविरलैः शीतच्छायैर्मनोरमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned on every side by flocks of male cuckoos, with dense, glossy, pleasing foliage that gave cool shade."}},{"n":4,"text":"सरांसि च विचित्राणि प्रसन्नसलिलानि च ।\nकमलैः सोत्पलैस्तत्र भ्राजमानानि सर्वशः ।\nपश्यन्तश्चारुरूपाणि रेमिरे तत्र पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were wondrous lakes of clear water, shining everywhere with lotuses and water lilies, and the Pandavas enjoyed gazing at their beauty."}},{"n":5,"text":"पुण्यगन्धः सुखस्पर्शो ववौ तत्र समीरणः ।\nह्लादयन्पाण्डवान्सर्वान्सकृष्णान्सद्विजर्षभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A sweet-scented, pleasant-touching breeze blew there, cheering all the Pandavas, Krishna Draupadi, and the foremost brahmins."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततः पूर्वोत्तरो वायुः पवमानो यदृच्छया ।\nसहस्रपत्रमर्काभं दिव्यं पद्ममुदावहत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a wind from the northeast, blowing as it chanced, carried along a divine thousand-petalled lotus that shone like the sun."}},{"n":7,"text":"तदपश्यत पाञ्चाली दिव्यगन्धं मनोरमम् ।\nअनिलेनाहृतं भूमौ पतितं जलजं शुचि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Panchali saw that fragrant, lovely, pure water flower, borne by the wind, fallen on the ground."}},{"n":8,"text":"तच्छुभा शुभमासाद्य सौगन्धिकमनुत्तमम् ।\nअतीव मुदिता राजन्भीमसेनमथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fair lady took that matchless saugandhika blossom and, greatly delighted, spoke to Bhimasena, O king."}},{"n":9,"text":"पश्य दिव्यं सुरुचिरं भीम पुष्पमनुत्तमम् ।\nगन्धसंस्थानसंपन्नं मनसो मम नन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She said: \"Look, Bhima, at this divine, radiant, peerless flower, so perfect in scent and shape, a joy to my heart.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"एतत्तु धर्मराजाय प्रदास्यामि परंतप ।\nहरेरिदं मे कामाय काम्यके पुनराश्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Scourge of foes, I shall offer this to Yudhishthira, the king of dharma. Bring it for my wish, that I may have it again in the hermitage at Kamyaka.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"यदि तेऽहं प्रिया पार्थ बहूनीमान्युपाहर ।\nतान्यहं नेतुमिच्छामि काम्यकं पुनराश्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I am dear to you, son of Pritha, fetch me many of these. I want to carry them to the Kamyaka hermitage.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु पाञ्चाली भीमसेनमनिन्दिता ।\nजगाम धर्मराजाय पुष्पमादाय तत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, blameless Panchali took the flower and went to Yudhishthira at once."}},{"n":13,"text":"अभिप्रायं तु विज्ञाय महिष्याः पुरुषर्षभः ।\nप्रियायाः प्रियकामः स भीमो भीमपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding his queen's wish, Bhima, the best of men, fearsome in prowess and eager to please his beloved, resolved to act."}},{"n":14,"text":"वातं तमेवाभिमुखो यतस्तत्पुष्पमागतम् ।\nआजिहीर्षुर्जगामाशु स पुष्पाण्यपराण्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Facing the very wind from which the flower had come, he hurried off to fetch more such flowers."}},{"n":15,"text":"रुक्मपृष्ठं धनुर्गृह्य शरांश्चाशीविषोपमान् ।\nमृगराडिव संक्रुद्धः प्रभिन्न इव कुञ्जरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took his gold-backed bow and arrows like venomous snakes, and went like an enraged lion or a rutting elephant."}},{"n":16,"text":"द्रौपद्याः प्रियमन्विच्छन्स्वबाहुबलमाश्रितः ।\nव्यपेतभयसंमोहः शैलमभ्यपतद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeking to please Draupadi, relying on the strength of his own arms, the mighty one charged up the mountain free of fear and confusion."}},{"n":17,"text":"स तं द्रुमलतागुल्मच्छन्नं नीलशिलातलम् ।\nगिरिं चचारारिहरः किंनराचरितं शुभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That slayer of enemies roamed the beautiful mountain, haunted by Kinnaras, its dark rock surfaces hidden by trees, creepers and thickets."}},{"n":18,"text":"नानावर्णधरैश्चित्रं धातुद्रुममृगाण्डजैः ।\nसर्वभूषणसंपूर्णं भूमेर्भुजमिवोच्छ्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was colourful with mineral-bright trees, beasts and birds of many hues, and full of every ornament, like the raised arm of the earth."}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वर्तुरमणीयेषु गन्धमादनसानुषु ।\nसक्तचक्षुरभिप्रायं हृदयेनानुचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His eyes fixed on the slopes of Gandhamadana, lovely in every season, he pondered in his heart what Draupadi wanted."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुंस्कोकिलनिनादेषु षट्पदाभिरुतेषु च ।\nबद्धश्रोत्रमनश्चक्षुर्जगामामितविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The boundlessly valiant one went with ear, mind and eye absorbed in the calls of male cuckoos and the humming of bees."}},{"n":21,"text":"जिघ्रमाणो महातेजाः सर्वर्तुकुसुमोद्भवम् ।\nगन्धमुद्दाममुद्दामो वने मत्त इव द्विपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty and splendid, he drank in the strong scent of flowers of every season, wild in the forest like a rutting elephant."}},{"n":22,"text":"ह्रियमाणश्रमः पित्रा संप्रहृष्टतनूरुहः ।\nपितुः संस्पर्शशीतेन गन्धमादनवायुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"His fatigue was taken away by his father, and the hair on his body thrilled at the Gandhamadana breeze, cool with his father's touch."}},{"n":23,"text":"स यक्षगन्धर्वसुरब्रह्मर्षिगणसेवितम् ।\nविलोडयामास तदा पुष्पहेतोररिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That tamer of foes searched through the mountain, frequented by Yakshas, Gandharvas, gods and brahmin sages, in quest of the flowers."}},{"n":24,"text":"विषमच्छेदरचितैरनुलिप्तमिवाङ्गुलैः ।\nविमलैर्धातुविच्छेदैः काञ्चनाञ्जनराजतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It looked as if smeared with finger-marks in uneven streaks, by clear bands of minerals, gold, collyrium and silver."}},{"n":25,"text":"सपक्षमिव नृत्यन्तं पार्श्वलग्नैः पयोधरैः ।\nमुक्ताहारैरिव चितं च्युतैः प्रस्रवणोदकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its clouds clung to its sides as if it were a winged dancer, and fallen streams seemed strings of pearls laid over it."}},{"n":26,"text":"अभिरामनदीकुञ्जनिर्झरोदरकन्दरम् ।\nअप्सरोनूपुररवैः प्रनृत्तबहुबर्हिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It had delightful river groves, waterfalls, hollows and caves, and many peacocks danced there to the anklet-sounds of Apsarases."}},{"n":27,"text":"दिग्वारणविषाणाग्रैर्घृष्टोपलशिलातलम् ।\nस्रस्तांशुकमिवाक्षोभ्यैर्निम्नगानिःसृतैर्जलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its rocky surfaces were rubbed by the tusk-tips of the elephants of the quarters, and its streams of water seemed a slipped garment that nothing could disturb."}},{"n":28,"text":"सशष्पकवलैः स्वस्थैरदूरपरिवर्तिभिः ।\nभयस्याज्ञैश्च हरिणैः कौतूहलनिरीक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deer that were healthy, grazing on grass nearby and unafraid, watched him with curiosity."}},{"n":29,"text":"चालयन्नूरुवेगेन लताजालान्यनेकशः ।\nआक्रीडमानः कौन्तेयः श्रीमान्वायुसुतो ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The glorious son of Kunti and of the Wind shook many nets of creepers with the speed of his thighs as he went playfully along."}},{"n":30,"text":"प्रियामनोरथं कर्तुमुद्यतश्चारुलोचनः ।\nप्रांशुः कनकतालाभः सिंहसंहननो युवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed, tall, golden as a palm tree, lion-bodied and young, he was set on fulfilling his beloved's wish."}},{"n":31,"text":"मत्तवारणविक्रान्तो मत्तवारणवेगवान् ।\nमत्तवारणताम्राक्षो मत्तवारणवारणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He strode like a rutting elephant, moved with the speed of one, had red eyes like one, and could stop such an elephant."}},{"n":32,"text":"प्रियपार्श्वोपविष्टाभिर्व्यावृत्ताभिर्विचेष्टितैः ।\nयक्षगन्धर्वयोषाभिरदृश्याभिर्निरीक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unseen Yaksha and Gandharva women, seated by their lovers and turning with eager gestures, gazed at him."}},{"n":33,"text":"नवावतारं रूपस्य विक्रीणन्निव पाण्डवः ।\nचचार रमणीयेषु गन्धमादनसानुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava seemed to be offering for sale a fresh arrival of beauty as he wandered the lovely slopes of Gandhamadana."}},{"n":34,"text":"संस्मरन्विविधान्क्लेशान्दुर्योधनकृतान्बहून् ।\nद्रौपद्या वनवासिन्याः प्रियं कर्तुं समुद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering the many sufferings Duryodhana had inflicted, he was set on pleasing Draupadi, who lived in the forest."}},{"n":35,"text":"सोऽचिन्तयद्गते स्वर्गमर्जुने मयि चागते ।\nपुष्पहेतोः कथं न्वार्यः करिष्यति युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thought: \"Now that Arjuna has gone to heaven and I have come here, how will noble Yudhishthira manage about the flowers?\""}},{"n":36,"text":"स्नेहान्नरवरो नूनमविश्वासाद्वनस्य च ।\nनकुलं सहदेवं च न मोक्ष्यति युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Out of affection, and from distrust of the forest, the best of men will surely not let Nakula and Sahadeva go.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"कथं नु कुसुमावाप्तिः स्याच्छीघ्रमिति चिन्तयन् ।\nप्रतस्थे नरशार्दूलः पक्षिराडिव वेगितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wondering how to get the flowers quickly, the tiger among men set off, swift as the king of birds."}},{"n":38,"text":"कम्पयन्मेदिनीं पद्भ्यां निर्घात इव पर्वसु ।\nत्रासयन्गजयूथानि वातरंहा वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaking the earth with his feet like a thunderclap at the turn of a season, scaring herds of elephants, Vrikodara went with the speed of the wind."}},{"n":39,"text":"सिंहव्याघ्रगणांश्चैव मर्दमानो महाबलः ।\nउन्मूलयन्महावृक्षान्पोथयंश्चोरसा बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one trampled troops of lions and tigers, uprooted great trees and struck them down with his chest."}},{"n":40,"text":"लतावल्लीश्च वेगेन विकर्षन्पाण्डुनन्दनः ।\nउपर्युपरि शैलाग्रमारुरुक्षुरिव द्विपः ।\nविनर्दमानोऽतिभृशं सविद्युदिव तोयदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Pandu dragged away creepers and vines at speed, like an elephant bent on climbing the mountain peaks, roaring loudly like a cloud with lightning."}},{"n":41,"text":"तस्य शब्देन घोरेण धनुर्घोषेण चाभिभो ।\nत्रस्तानि मृगयूथानि समन्ताद्विप्रदुद्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his dreadful cry and the twang of his bow, lord, herds of deer fled in terror in every direction."}},{"n":42,"text":"अथापश्यन्महाबाहुर्गन्धमादनसानुषु ।\nसुरम्यं कदलीषण्डं बहुयोजनविस्तृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the long-armed one saw on the slopes of Gandhamadana a lovely plantain grove stretching many yojanas."}},{"n":43,"text":"तमभ्यगच्छद्वेगेन क्षोभयिष्यन्महाबलः ।\nमहागज इवास्रावी प्रभञ्जन्विविधान्द्रुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The very strong one rushed at it to churn it up, like a great rutting elephant breaking many kinds of trees."}},{"n":44,"text":"उत्पाट्य कदलीस्कन्धान्बहुतालसमुच्छ्रयान् ।\nचिक्षेप तरसा भीमः समन्ताद्बलिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, best of the strong, tore up plantain trunks as tall as many palms and hurled them violently all around."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः सत्त्वान्युपाक्रामन्बहूनि च महान्ति च ।\nरुरुवारणसंघाश्च महिषाश्च जलाश्रयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then many large creatures attacked, herds of ruru deer and elephants, and buffaloes that live in water."}},{"n":46,"text":"सिंहव्याघ्राश्च संक्रुद्धा भीमसेनमभिद्रवन् ।\nव्यादितास्या महारौद्रा विनदन्तोऽतिभीषणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious lions and tigers rushed at Bhimasena, jaws wide open, terrible and roaring fearfully."}},{"n":47,"text":"ततो वायुसुतः क्रोधात्स्वबाहुबलमाश्रितः ।\nगजेनाघ्नन्गजं भीमः सिंहं सिंहेन चाभिभूः ।\nतलप्रहारैरन्यांश्च व्यहनत्पाण्डवो बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Wind's son, in anger, relying on his own arm's strength, killed an elephant with an elephant and a lion with a lion, and the mighty Pandava struck down others with blows of his palm."}},{"n":48,"text":"ते हन्यमाना भीमेन सिंहव्याघ्रतरक्षवः ।\nभयाद्विससृपुः सर्वे शकृन्मूत्रं च सुस्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beaten by Bhima, the lions, tigers and hyenas slunk away in fear and loosed their dung and urine."}},{"n":49,"text":"प्रविवेश ततः क्षिप्रं तानपास्य महाबलः ।\nवनं पाण्डुसुतः श्रीमाञ्शब्देनापूरयन्दिशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thrust them aside, the mighty and glorious son of Pandu quickly entered the forest, filling the directions with his roar."}},{"n":50,"text":"तेन शब्देन चोग्रेण भीमसेनरवेण च ।\nवनान्तरगताः सर्वे वित्रेसुर्मृगपक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that fierce sound and Bhimasena's cry, all the beasts and birds in the depth of the forest were terrified."}},{"n":51,"text":"तं शब्दं सहसा श्रुत्वा मृगपक्षिसमीरितम् ।\nजलार्द्रपक्षा विहगाः समुत्पेतुः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that sudden noise raised by the animals, thousands of water birds with wet wings flew up."}},{"n":52,"text":"तानौदकान्पक्षिगणान्निरीक्ष्य भरतर्षभः ।\nतानेवानुसरन्रम्यं ददर्श सुमहत्सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those water birds, the bull of the Bharatas followed them and saw a very large, lovely lake."}},{"n":53,"text":"काञ्चनैः कदलीषण्डैर्मन्दमारुतकम्पितैः ।\nवीज्यमानमिवाक्षोभ्यं तीरान्तरविसर्पिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was fanned, as it were, by golden plantain groves stirred by a gentle breeze and spreading along the shores, and it stayed calm."}},{"n":54,"text":"तत्सरोऽथावतीर्याशु प्रभूतकमलोत्पलम् ।\nमहागज इवोद्दामश्चिक्रीड बलवद्बली ।\nविक्रीड्य तस्मिन्सुचिरमुत्ततारामितद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima quickly went into that lake full of lotuses and water lilies and played, strong and unrestrained, like a great elephant. After sporting there long, the one of boundless splendour came out."}},{"n":55,"text":"ततोऽवगाह्य वेगेन तद्वनं बहुपादपम् ।\nदध्मौ च शङ्खं स्वनवत्सर्वप्राणेन पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava plunged quickly into the forest of many trees and blew his conch with all his breath, making it resound."}},{"n":56,"text":"तस्य शङ्खस्य शब्देन भीमसेनरवेण च ।\nबाहुशब्देन चोग्रेण नर्दन्तीव गिरेर्गुहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the sound of the conch, Bhimasena's cry and the fierce slap of his arms, the mountain's caves seemed to roar."}},{"n":57,"text":"तं वज्रनिष्पेषसममास्फोटितरवं भृशम् ।\nश्रुत्वा शैलगुहासुप्तैः सिंहैर्मुक्तो महास्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that din, like the crash of a thunderbolt and the slapping of arms, lions sleeping in the mountain caves let out a great roar."}},{"n":58,"text":"सिंहनादभयत्रस्तैः कुञ्जरैरपि भारत ।\nमुक्तो विरावः सुमहान्पर्वतो येन पूरितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants too, frightened by the lions' roar, bellowed, Bharata, and the mountain was filled with the great noise."}},{"n":59,"text":"तं तु नादं ततः श्रुत्वा सुप्तो वानरपुंगवः ।\nप्राजृम्भत महाकायो हनूमान्नाम वानरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that sound, a great monkey who lay asleep woke and yawned, a huge-bodied ape named Hanuman."}},{"n":60,"text":"कदलीषण्डमध्यस्थो निद्रावशगतस्तदा ।\nजृम्भमाणः सुविपुलं शक्रध्वजमिवोच्छ्रितम् ।\nआस्फोटयत लाङ्गूलमिन्द्राशनिसमस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lying asleep in the middle of the plantain grove, he stretched, and lashed his vast tail, raised like Indra's banner, with a crack like Indra's thunderbolt."}},{"n":61,"text":"तस्य लाङ्गूलनिनदं पर्वतः स गुहामुखैः ।\nउद्गारमिव गौर्नर्दमुत्ससर्ज समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mountain, through its cave mouths, gave back the thunder of that tail on every side, as a cow gives out a bellow."}},{"n":62,"text":"स लाङ्गूलरवस्तस्य मत्तवारणनिस्वनम् ।\nअन्तर्धाय विचित्रेषु चचार गिरिसानुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tail's sound drowned the trumpeting of the rutting elephants and travelled over the varied mountain slopes."}},{"n":63,"text":"स भीमसेनस्तं श्रुत्वा संप्रहृष्टतनूरुहः ।\nशब्दप्रभवमन्विच्छंश्चचार कदलीवनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing it, Bhimasena, with the hair on his body thrilled, went through the plantain grove looking for the source of the sound."}},{"n":64,"text":"कदलीवनमध्यस्थमथ पीने शिलातले ।\nस ददर्श महाबाहुर्वानराधिपतिं स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of the plantain grove, on a broad rock slab, the long-armed Bhima saw the lord of the monkeys lying."}},{"n":65,"text":"विद्युत्संघातदुष्प्रेक्ष्यं विद्युत्संघातपिङ्गलम् ।\nविद्युत्संघातसदृशं विद्युत्संघातचञ्चलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was hard to look at like a mass of lightning, tawny as lightning, like lightning in appearance and as quick as lightning."}},{"n":66,"text":"बाहुस्वस्तिकविन्यस्तपीनह्रस्वशिरोधरम् ।\nस्कन्धभूयिष्ठकायत्वात्तनुमध्यकटीतटम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His thick, short neck rested on his folded arms, and because his shoulders were so heavy, his waist and hips seemed slender."}},{"n":67,"text":"किंचिच्चाभुग्नशीर्षेण दीर्घरोमाञ्चितेन च ।\nलाङ्गूलेनोर्ध्वगतिना ध्वजेनेव विराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His head was a little bowed, his hair long and bristling, and his tail, rising upward, shone like a banner."}},{"n":68,"text":"रक्तोष्ठं ताम्रजिह्वास्यं रक्तकर्णं चलद्भ्रुवम् ।\nवदनं वृत्तदंष्ट्राग्रं रश्मिवन्तमिवोडुपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His lips were red, his tongue and mouth copper-coloured, his ears red and his brows moving, his face round-fanged, like a moon with rays."}},{"n":69,"text":"वदनाभ्यन्तरगतैः शुक्लभासैरलंकृतम् ।\nकेसरोत्करसंमिश्रमशोकानामिवोत्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His mouth was adorned with gleaming white teeth, like a heap of ashoka flowers mixed with filaments."}},{"n":70,"text":"हिरण्मयीनां मध्यस्थं कदलीनां महाद्युतिम् ।\nदीप्यमानं स्ववपुषा अर्चिष्मन्तमिवानलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the midst of golden plantains, of great radiance, he blazed with his own body like a flaming fire."}},{"n":71,"text":"निरीक्षन्तमवित्रस्तं लोचनैर्मधुपिङ्गलैः ।\nतं वानरवरं वीरमतिकायं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He looked on without fear, with honey-tawny eyes, that heroic best of monkeys, huge-bodied and very strong."}},{"n":72,"text":"अथोपसृत्य तरसा भीमो भीमपराक्रमः ।\nसिंहनादं समकरोद्बोधयिष्यन्कपिं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, terrible in prowess, rushed up and gave a lion's roar, wanting to wake the monkey."}},{"n":73,"text":"तेन शब्देन भीमस्य वित्रेसुर्मृगपक्षिणः ।\nहनूमांश्च महासत्त्व ईषदुन्मील्य लोचने ।\nअवैक्षदथ सावज्ञं लोचनैर्मधुपिङ्गलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that cry of Bhima the beasts and birds trembled, and the mighty Hanuman half opened his eyes and looked at him with contempt, with his honey-tawny eyes."}},{"n":74,"text":"स्मितेनाभाष्य कौन्तेयं वानरो नरमब्रवीत् ।\nकिमर्थं सरुजस्तेऽहं सुखसुप्तः प्रबोधितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The monkey spoke to the son of Kunti with a smile: \"Why have you woken me, ill as I am, from a happy sleep?\""}},{"n":75,"text":"ननु नाम त्वया कार्या दया भूतेषु जानता ।\nवयं धर्मं न जानीमस्तिर्यग्योनिं समाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You should show compassion to creatures, since you know better. We do not know dharma, being born in animal wombs.\""}},{"n":76,"text":"मनुष्या बुद्धिसंपन्ना दयां कुर्वन्ति जन्तुषु ।\nक्रूरेषु कर्मसु कथं देहवाक्चित्तदूषिषु ।\nधर्मघातिषु सज्जन्ते बुद्धिमन्तो भवद्विधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Humans are endowed with understanding and show kindness to beasts. How can wise men like you take to cruel deeds that foul body, speech and mind and destroy dharma?\""}},{"n":77,"text":"न त्वं धर्मं विजानासि वृद्धा नोपासितास्त्वया ।\nअल्पबुद्धितया वन्यानुत्सादयसि यन्मृगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You do not know dharma, and you have not served the old. In your small understanding you are destroying the forest deer.\""}},{"n":78,"text":"ब्रूहि कस्त्वं किमर्थं वा वनं त्वमिदमागतः ।\nवर्जितं मानुषैर्भावैस्तथैव पुरुषैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me who you are and why you have come into this forest, which is free of human ways and of human beings.\""}},{"n":79,"text":"अतः परमगम्योऽयं पर्वतः सुदुरारुहः ।\nविना सिद्धगतिं वीर गतिरत्र न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Beyond this, the mountain is impassable and very hard to climb. Without the attainment of the perfected ones, hero, there is no way here.\""}},{"n":80,"text":"कारुण्यात्सौहृदाच्चैव वारये त्वां महाबल ।\nनातः परं त्वया शक्यं गन्तुमाश्वसिहि प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Out of pity and friendship I hold you back, mighty one. You cannot go further than this; be calm, lord.\""}},{"n":81,"text":"इमान्यमृतकल्पानि मूलानि च फलानि च ।\nभक्षयित्वा निवर्तस्व ग्राह्यं यदि वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Eat these roots and fruits, which are like nectar, and turn back, if you will take my word.\""}}]}]}